I haven't changed `accounts/session.go`. AGENTS.md requires asking before I change code linked to a risk-controlling item, and `Login` is one.

**Linked items for `Login`:**
- **R-LOGIN-LOCKOUT** (`trace/requirements.yaml`) refines N-ACCOUNT-SAFE and **controls RISK-ACCOUNT-TAKEOVER**. Its code link is `accounts/session.go#Sessions.Login`, and its test is `TestLoginLockout` in `accounts/session_test.go`.
- R-PASSWORD-HASH and R-SESSION-EXPIRY are not linked to `Login` in code. R-PASSWORD-HASH's test, `TestLogin`, does exercise `Login`.

Your change keeps R-LOGIN-LOCKOUT true. The lockout still refuses the right password for 15 minutes, and the hash is only computed earlier. The change does touch an item that controls a risk, so please confirm before I make it.

**Proposed change** (the body of `Login`, after the lookup and `now := s.now()`):

```go
	c, ok := s.byEmail[email]
	if !ok {
		return "", ErrBadCredentials
	}
	now := s.now()
	hash, err := hashPassword(password, c.salt)
	if err != nil {
		return "", err
	}
	if now.Before(c.lockedUntil) {
		return "", ErrLocked
	}
	if subtle.ConstantTimeCompare(hash, c.hash) != 1 {
		// unchanged
```

Once you approve, I'll make this change and run `go test ./accounts/...`, which covers `TestLoginLockout`, `TestLogin` and `TestSessionExpiry`.

**Gap you may want to decide on:** an unknown email still returns before any hashing, so timing still reveals whether an email is registered. Fixing that would need a dummy hash for unknown emails, in the same function and under the same item, so it needs your approval too. I have left it out of the proposal.
